  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/apareiodon-affinis-2/",
      "html": "<p>Apareiodon affinis grows to a maximum length of 15 cm and should be kept in a group of 5 specimens upwards.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/apareiodon-affinis-2/",
      "html": "<p>Originally the species was described as Parodon affinis. It is amazingly similar in shape and coloration to the Asian Flying Foxes; but of course, the La Plata algae eater can always be easily recognized by the tetra-typical adipose fin that flying foxes always lack.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/apareiodon-affinis-2/",
      "html": "<p>The species comes from Paraguay.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/apareiodon-affinis-2/",
      "html": "<p>The fish are out all day looking for food. Against conspecifics and non-species fish the La Plata algae eater is completely peaceful.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/apareiodon-affinis-2/",
      "html": "<p>Since they are subtropical fish, they can be kept in a wide range of temperatures (16-28°C), but sudden changes in temperature are just as harmful as keeping them constantly above 26°C for a long time (more than half a year).</p><p>The chemical composition of the water is irrelevant for the care of the animals, but it should be clean and rich in oxygen.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/apareiodon-affinis-2/",
      "html": "<p>Besides algae they also consume any common fish food.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/apareiodon-affinis-2/",
      "html": "<p>Should be kept in a group of 5 specimens upwards. Completely peaceful towards conspecifics and other fish.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/apareiodon-affinis-2/",
      "html": "<p>Lexicon: Apareiodon means \"without teeth on the side of the mouth\". Parodon means \"with the same teeth\". affinis means \"similar\".</p>"
    }
  ],
